-- title:
--   Gauss centre on the j-finite chart specialises to the cusp
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\operatorname{coeffEmb} L$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field $\operatorname{x1FunctionFieldC} \mathbb{Q} (\Gamma_1(Mp)) \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} \mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion $\operatorname{coeffEmb} L(q^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{jNumQ})$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ characterised by: $f \in W_0$ exactly when there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ as Laurent series over $L$. Let $\psi$ be a ring homomorphism from the algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$ to $A$ whose composite with $A \to L$ computes the $0$-th Laurent coefficient, and let $\varepsilon$ be $\operatorname{Spec} \psi$ followed by the chart inclusion $\operatorname{ι Inf}$ into the two-chart model, the pushout of the two morphisms from the middle chart to the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite charts. Then there is a point $y_0$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ such that, for $a$ in that algebra, $a$ lies in the prime $y_0$ exactly when $a$ lies in the set of nonunits of $W_0$, and the image of $y_0$ under the base map of $\operatorname{ι Fin}$ specialises to the image of the closed point of $A$ under the base map of $\varepsilon$.
--
--   This is the chart-transfer step identifying the point of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ cut out by the Gauss valuation (the centre of $W_0$) as a point whose closure contains the reduction of the cusp $\infty$, the latter being given by the constant-term homomorphism on the $j^{-1}$-finite chart. It is used in identifying the valuation subring of $K$ attached to the stalk at that cusp with the Gauss ring $W_0$.
-- source:
